  <data name="HomePage_Poems" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Light—cosmic dot; black hole its plotted ellipsis.
Screens fake light with filters, like résumés fake life.
If light is speech, the rainbow is its slang.
Low is no abyss; it's where light learns to swerve.
If dark is light's dead end, what waits beyond the end?
Light—postcard from space; stars are the stamps it collects.
Cities pin neon to night, like hearts to bottled notes.
If light's the courier, dusk is its return address.
Alone is no abyss; it's light rehearsing tongue-twisters in echoes.
If shadows are light's reflection, who peers at the mirror's end?
Light—time's pencil; sunset keeps its point.
Chrome fakes dawn like emojis fake heartbeats.
If light's a dialect, auroras are its archaic tongue.
Night is no finish; it's light's blank draft.
If silence is light's antonym, who reads beyond the antonym?
Light—galaxy's comma; meteors its bold italics.
We cage light in screens like birds hung beneath clouds.
If light's a code, fireflies tap its Morse.
Fog is no wall; it's light training to vanish.
If dust is shattered light, who pieces the jigsaw's end?
Light—eraser of years; wrinkles the pencil crumbs it leaves.
Flashes fake forever like screenshots fake tears.
If light's a tune, dawn is its prelude.
Ruins aren't the end; light hatches echoes there.
If echoes are light's shadow, who calls at the shadow's edge?
Light—cosmic sticky note; supernovas its ripped-off exclamation.
We fold light into billboards like poems folded into cash.
If light's a cipher, moonlight is its whisper.
Rain is no glitch; it's light self-filtering.
If the end is light's riddle, who sets the riddle past the end?
Why not try XIGUA Security?</value>
  </data>
